1 counted   A, then B   [the home: B: a copy is needed]
0 counted   A, then B, then A   [the home: A: no copy is needed]
1 counted   A, then B, then A, then B   [the home: B: a copy is needed]
0 counted   A, then a write that covers the block in part   [the home: not known]
0 counted   A, then B, then a write that covers it in part   [the home: not known (B in part at least, or A again)]
1 counted   A, then a write in part, then B whole   [the home: B: a copy is needed]
0 counted   A, then a write-zeroes   [the home: zeros: a copy is needed]
0 counted   A, then B, then a write-zeroes   [the home: zeros: a copy is needed]
0 counted   zeros, then B, then a write-zeroes   [the home: zeros: no copy is needed]
1 counted   A, then a write-zeroes, then B received after it   [the home: B: a copy is needed]
1 counted   zeros; B is received, then a write-zeroes over it, then B is applied (the store runs B first: records_of puts the write-zeroes at its receipt and calls the block ambiguous)   [the home: zeros: no copy is needed]
